   "path": "SCENE.md",
   "role": "instructions",
   "content": "# Glass Notification Aurora\n\nTwo frosted-glass notification cards slide over a slowly moving aurora backdrop: one fills a progress bar and flips to done, the other types a reply.\n\nCategory: ui-blocks. Length: 8 s. WebGL: yes.\n\nUse when:\n- Notification cards should feel premium and float over a colourful animated backdrop.\n- A product or app moment (export done, new message) needs a glassy UI overlay.\n\nAvoid when:\n- The cards must refract the scene behind them like real glass: this block blurs and tints but does not bend it.\n- A flat, simple notification: use a plain notification block.\n\nVariables:\n- card1_title (string): First card title, default \"Export\"\n- card1_status (string): First card status, default \"rendering\"\n- card1_status_done (string): First card done status, default \"complete\"\n- card1_text (string): First card text, default \"Your video preview is encoding.\"\n- card1_text_done (string): First card done text, default \"promo-final.mp4 is ready.\"\n- card2_title (string): Second card title, default \"Messages\"\n- card2_text (string): Second card text, default \"Miguel: can it feel alive but still native?\"\n- chip_1 (string): Action chip 1, default \"Reply\"\n- chip_2 (string): Action chip 2, default \"Mark Read\"\n- resolution (number, 0.25-1): Resolution, default 0.5\n\nSource: heygen-com/hyperframes. Licence: Apache-2.0. The scene file keeps the upstream notice.\n"
  },
